      "writtenOn": "2023-08-30T08:53:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is quite error-prone; especially since it would also fail at runtime, not build time.\n\nMaybe one way to make it a bit less confusing is to call it connectivity-net-module-utils-bpf-minus-struct ? But it doesn\u0027t scale very well.\n\nAnd/or maybe restrict it via \"visibility\", and have a comment there saying that any new user needs to make sure they have the \"struct\" dep somewhere ? It\u0027s still error-prone when you\u0027d think you can remove the dependency on \"struct\" from framework-connectivity, but you actually can\u0027t.\n\nIf this was only used by service-connectivity, it would make sense for this lib to depend on framework-connectivity-pre-jarjar, to have all hidden utils in the bootclasspath from framework-connectivity. But because it\u0027s also used in Tethering that is R+, it needs to cherry-pick only libs that are included in both...",
